HYBRID GATE — credits and provenance

Data: the MNIST database of handwritten digits, Y. LeCun, C. Cortes and C. J. C. Burges, licensed CC BY-SA 3.0, from
Google's public mirror (storage.googleapis.com/cvdf-datasets/mnist). data/mnist/ holds the four files unchanged; their
SHA-256 hashes are sealed in CLAIMS.md. The files keep their CC BY-SA 3.0 licence.

The cell kernel, the seeded rng and SHA-256 are Rung 1, sjgant80-hub/settling-cell, vendored byte for byte under
vendor/settling-cell/. The cell's energy follows Hopfield (1982) and Krotov & Hopfield (2016). The check digit is
H. P. Luhn's (US patent 2,950,048, 1960).

Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin.

